W: 2. Immortal and divine
W: Great Bacchus, god of wine
W: Create me by adoption your own son
W: In hopes that you’ll comply
W: That my glass shall ne’er run dry
W: Nor my darlin’ little cruiscín lán, lán, lán
W: My darlin’ little cruiscín lán.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Oh, gradh mo chroide mo cruiscín
W: (Oh, graw moh kree moh krooshkeen)
W: Slainte geal Mauverneen
W: (Slawnta gal Mohvoorneen)
W: Gradh mo chroide mo cruiscín lán, lán, lán
W: (Graw moh kree moh krooshkeen lawn, lawn, lawn)
W: Oh, gradh mo chroide mo cruiscín lán
W: (Oh, graw moh kree moh krooshkeen lawn)
W:
W: 3. Oh, when cruel death appears
W: In a few but happy years
W: You’ll say: “Oh, won’t you come along with me?”
W: I’ll say: “Begone, you knave,
W: For King Bacchus gave me lave
W: To take another cruiscín lán, lán, lán
W: To take another cruiscín lán.” (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Then fill your glasses high
W: Let’s not part with lips so dry
W: For the lark now proclaims it is the dawn
W: And since we can’t remain
W: May we shortly meet again
W: To fill another cruiscín lán, lán, lán
W: To fill another cruiscín lán. (Chorus)
